window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-5e992debb47ae256"]={"key":"ny_b1-5e992debb47ae256","group":"ny_b1","uid":"5e992debb47ae256","rank":4,"title":"marchmont franchise nonrenewal memorandum","occupation":"general_operations_managers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are the general and operations manager at Marchmont Coffee Houses, preparing a sensitive package for Perpetua Odell after President Idris Vanterpool approved the decision not to renew her two franchise agreements when they expire in March. She has operated the locations for twelve years, but the last two review cycles were poor after her husband's illness, and I need a document that lets her understand the decision and act on her remaining options rather than simply close the doors. Prepare `marchmont_nonrenewal_buyout_memorandum.docx` and place it at the top level of the working directory, using exactly that filename. The document will be read first by Perpetua, then by Idris, Bianca Boateng at Wrenfield Associates, and reviewers at the Yewbank Regional Office; Ibrahim Skarsgard, Stellan Achterberg, Fatou Elbaz, and Theo Kristiansen may also use it while coordinating the transition, so write for a mixed audience without turning the document into a tutorial. Keep the finished document to four pages or fewer and make it a polished memorandum that can be sent externally after a final factual review. Include the non-renewal notice for both agreements, the effective expiry date or dates, the business reason stated respectfully and without unnecessary personal detail, and a clear explanation of what the decision does and does not mean. Include a buyout valuation for each location and a combined figure, showing the basis of the estimate, the treatment of equipment or other holdbacks, the resulting amount payable or receivable, the assumptions used, and any figures that still require confirmation; do not present an estimate as a settled contractual entitlement. Include a transition timeline covering the period before expiry and the end state afterward, including the date on which point-of-sale access ends, the handling of inventory, equipment, records, signage, employee communications, outstanding customer obligations, and the handover of premises or operations. The document must make clear that a sale or transfer to another Marchmont franchisee remains open until the March expiry, while also making clear that this possibility is not a renewal and is not guaranteed. Give Perpetua a practical contact route and enough timing information to decide whether to pursue that option, obtain advice, or wind down. Use a calm, direct tone: acknowledge the twelve-year relationship, avoid blaming her husband's illness, do not lead with the valuation table, and do not imply that a review-cycle improvement would reverse the approved decision. Number the requirements in the document if that helps the reader locate them, but do not include internal drafting commentary, unsupported legal conclusions, invented policy citations, or claims about rights and remedies that are not established by the information available. End with the decision and the available path through expiry, not with a generic list of future work. Before delivering it, check that every amount, date, location, option, access cutoff, and stated conclusion agrees everywhere it appears.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `marchmont_nonrenewal_buyout_memorandum.docx` — A polished external-facing memorandum containing the non-renewal notice, buyout valuation, assumptions and holdback treatment, and transition timeline for both Marchmont Coffee Houses franchise locations. (Must be no more than four pages when rendered.; Must use exactly the specified filename and be written to the top level of the working directory.; Must be suitable for both the franchisee and oversight review.; Must distinguish confirmed facts from estimates, assumptions, and items requiring confirmation.; Must keep all dates, amounts, options, locations, and operational cutoffs internally consistent.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/marchmont_nonrenewal_buyout_memorandum.docx","bytes":41867,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/38d5dc20866a67621e191a8d73e0b5091019a8ed85cbd5b30f0f956ed8b17fa0.docx","sha256":"38d5dc20866a67621e191a8d73e0b5091019a8ed85cbd5b30f0f956ed8b17fa0","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"MEMORANDUM\nNotice of Non-Renewal and Transition Framework\nTo\nPerpetua Odell, Franchisee\nFrom\nMarchmont Coffee Houses | Franchise Operations\nDate\n9 January 2026\nSubject\nWillowmere Station and Kingsway Market franchise agreements\nPerpetua,\nMarchmont recognizes your twelve years of operating the Willowmere Station and Kingsway Market coffee houses. This memorandum gives formal notice of the approved decision, an indicative buyout estimate, and a practical path through expiry. It is intended to support an orderly decision and transition; it is not a substitute for the agreements or for advice you may wish to obtain.\n1. Formal notice and scope\nConfirmed decision. President Idris Vanterpool has approved the decision that Marchmont Coffee Houses will not renew either of your franchise agreements: Willowmere Station and Kingsway Market. Both agreements expire on 31 March 2026, and no renewal is being offered after that date.\nBusiness context. The decision follows the two poor review cycles and the need for a clear operating outcome for both locations. We acknowledge that the recent period has been difficult without assigning personal circumstances as a reason or fault. The approved decision is final for these agreements; a later review-cycle improvement would not change the non-renewal.\nWhat this does and does not mean. You may continue operating under the existing agreements through 31 March 2026, subject to their existing terms. This notice concerns non-renewal. It does not decide the final reconciliation of accounts, the treatment of any particular asset, or any matter that still requires confirmation.\n2. Available path through expiry\nTransfer remains open. A sale or transfer to another Marchmont franchisee may be pursued for either or both locations through the 31 March 2026 expiry. This is not a renewal of your agreements and is not guaranteed: a suitable recipient, required review, and timely completion would still be needed. To preserve a workable transition window, please tell us by 14 February 2026 if you want transfer discussions or an introduction process to be considered.\nContact and choice. For transfer discussions or questions on the estimate, contact Bianca Boateng at Wrenfield Associates through the Wrenfield case contact, with a copy to Marchmont Franchise Operations. You may also obtain independent advice. If you do not pursue a transfer, you may operate through expiry and follow the orderly wind-down and handover described below.\n3. Indicative buyout valuation\nEstimated only. The figures below are a transparent working estimate for discussion and planning, not a settled contractual entitlement, guaranteed payment, or final account. “Eligible” means the item is assumed capable of being included after confirmation; it does not decide ownership or final treatment.\nEstimated component (USD)\nWillowmere\nStation\nKingsway\nMarket\nCombined\nTransferable operating value\n$86,000\n$74,000\n$160,000\nEligible inventory at book cost\n$9,500\n$7,500\n$17,000\nEligible equipment value before inspection\n$24,000\n$18,500\n$42,500\nLess: estimated open supplier/brand balance\n($6,500)\n($5,000)\n($11,500)\nProvisional gross amount\n$113,000\n$95,000\n$208,000\nLess: equipment holdback (20% of equipment)\n($4,800)\n($3,700)\n($8,500)\nProposed estimated amount payable\n$108,200\n$91,300\n$199,500\n\nValuation notes\nBasis and holdback. The estimate combines an indicative transferable operating value, counted inventory at book cost, and equipment assessed as eligible, less the stated estimated balances. The equipment holdback reserves 20% of the eligible equipment value pending condition inspection and return/transfer confirmation: $4,800 for Willowmere Station and $3,700 for Kingsway Market, reducing the provisional gross amount by $8,500 to the $199,500 combined estimated amount payable.\nAssumptions and confirmations needed. Assumptions are that both locations remain in normal operating condition through expiry, inventory is saleable, and the listed balances are complete. Before any settlement discussion, Marchmont and Perpetua should confirm the closing inventory count, equipment condition and ownership, returnable or company-owned equipment, outstanding supplier/brand balances, customer commitments, and the relevant agreement records. Equipment excluded because it is leased, loaned, or confirmed for return is not included as eligible equipment in this estimate.\n4. Transition schedule\nWhen\nOwner / trigger\nAction for both locations\nBy 14 Feb 2026\nPerpetua / Bianca Boateng\nTell Wrenfield Associates whether to explore transfer; identify any prospective Marchmont franchisee. Perpetua may obtain advice or choose orderly wind-down.\n17-27 Mar 2026\nPerpetua + Marchmont operations\nJoint inventory count; equipment inspection and return/transfer list; reconcile business records and data. Agree employee communication timing and a customer-obligation log for prepaid orders, gift instruments, loyalty balances, and open complaints.\nBy 30 Mar 2026\nMarchmont operations + Perpetua\nConfirm handover plan: premises condition, keys and access, signage and branded-material removal or transfer, and the named point of contact for outstanding customer obligations.\n31 Mar 2026, 6:00 p.m. local time\nExpiry / Perpetua\nExisting POS access ends. Complete turnover of operational records, keys, access credentials, and agreed equipment. Continue no brand-facing operation beyond the agreement expiry unless a separately completed transfer has taken effect.\nAfter 31 Mar 2026\nMarchmont operations\nEnd state: both agreements are not renewed; Perpetua has no POS access or authority to operate as these Marchmont locations. Marchmont will coordinate the confirmed premises/operations handover and route unresolved documented customer obligations for resolution.\n\nClosing. The decision is that the Willowmere Station and Kingsway Market agreements will not renew on 31 March 2026. Until then, the available path is a possible but unguaranteed transfer to another Marchmont franchisee, or an orderly wind-down and handover using this schedule; the valuation remains an estimate pending the listed confirmations.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"r01","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Marchmont Coffee Houses as the issuing organization.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered memorandum header or opening notice.","grader_hint":"Confirm the organization name appears as the issuer, not merely in background text."},{"rubric_item_id":"r02","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Perpetua Odell as the recipient or franchisee.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Addressing, salutation, or notice body.","grader_hint":"Check that the name is unambiguous and consistently spelled."},{"rubric_item_id":"r03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Idris Vanterpool or the president as the approving authority.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Notice or approval context.","grader_hint":"Accept either the named person with title or a clearly identified approval statement."},{"rubric_item_id":"r04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states that both franchise agreements will not be renewed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Formal notice language.","grader_hint":"Both agreements must be covered; a statement about only one location is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"r05","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The notice is unmistakably a non-renewal rather than a tentative review or invitation to renegotiate.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall notice wording.","grader_hint":"A reasonable recipient should understand that renewal is not being offered."},{"rubric_item_id":"r06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The expiry date or dates are stated concretely and agree with the March expiry described in the request.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Notice and timeline.","grader_hint":"Do not award for vague wording such as 'in March' alone when a precise date is supplied or chosen elsewhere."},{"rubric_item_id":"r07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"If the two agreements have different expiry dates, each date is tied to the correct location and both are used consistently.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Location table, notice, and timeline.","grader_hint":"If the document clearly establishes one common date, award when that common date is used consistently."},{"rubric_item_id":"r08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The opening frames the communication as a serious relationship-sensitive decision before presenting valuation figures.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Document sequence and opening paragraphs.","grader_hint":"The valuation table should not be the first substantive content."},{"rubric_item_id":"r09","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum acknowledges the twelve-year operating relationship.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening or closing relationship paragraph.","grader_hint":"A specific reference to twelve years is required."},{"rubric_item_id":"r10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The explanation of the decision is respectful, factual, and free of gratuitous personal detail about the illness.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reason-for-decision paragraphs.","grader_hint":"The poor review cycles may be referenced, but the illness must not be used as blame or sensational explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document refers to the two poor review cycles as part of the business context.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reason-for-decision section.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent wording such as two unfavorable review periods."},{"rubric_item_id":"r12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not imply that improving future reviews would reverse the approved non-renewal.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire document.","grader_hint":"Look for conditional or hopeful language that undermines the finality of the decision."},{"rubric_item_id":"r13","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The valuation covers each franchise location separately.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation table or clearly separated location subsections.","grader_hint":"A combined total alone does not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"r14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The combined valuation is mathematically consistent with the two location-level valuations, subject to explicitly disclosed adjustments.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation table and calculation notes.","grader_hint":"Recalculate the displayed components; any group-level adjustment must be named and included in the arithmetic."},{"rubric_item_id":"r15","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document labels the buyout figure as an estimate, valuation, or otherwise non-final calculation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation heading and explanatory text.","grader_hint":"The qualification must be proximate enough to prevent a reader treating it as a settled entitlement."},{"rubric_item_id":"r16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The valuation basis is understandable to a non-specialist reader without becoming a tutorial.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation explanation.","grader_hint":"Look for a concise explanation of what is being valued and why, not unexplained jargon or a long lesson."},{"rubric_item_id":"r17","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The valuation shows identifiable component categories rather than only a single unexplained total.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation table.","grader_hint":"Accept categories such as transferable business value, equipment, inventory, liabilities, or other clearly labeled components."},{"rubric_item_id":"r18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every displayed valuation subtotal equals the sum of its displayed components.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All valuation arithmetic.","grader_hint":"Recompute subtotals with a calculator or spreadsheet."},{"rubric_item_id":"r19","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document explains what the equipment holdback is.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation notes.","grader_hint":"The term must be explained in relation to the equipment and the amount retained or deducted."},{"rubric_item_id":"r20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The effect of the equipment holdback on the amount payable or receivable is shown numerically and agrees with the final amount.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation calculation.","grader_hint":"Trace the holdback from its stated amount or percentage through to the net result."},{"rubric_item_id":"r21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document distinguishes equipment included in the estimate from equipment subject to holdback, return, inspection, or confirmation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation and transition sections.","grader_hint":"Award only when the treatment is operationally meaningful, not merely a repeated label."},{"rubric_item_id":"r22","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies assumptions underlying the valuation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assumptions or calculation notes.","grader_hint":"Look for a distinct, readable statement of assumptions."},{"rubric_item_id":"r23","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies figures or facts that require confirmation before settlement.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Qualification notes.","grader_hint":"Examples may include equipment condition, inventory count, outstanding balances, or contractual review."},{"rubric_item_id":"r24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not represent unsupported valuation assumptions as established contractual rights or obligations.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation wording.","grader_hint":"Check whether the writer appropriately separates estimate, proposed amount, and confirmed amount."},{"rubric_item_id":"r25","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states that a sale or transfer to another Marchmont franchisee remains open until the March expiry.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Options paragraph and timeline.","grader_hint":"The availability window and the March endpoint must both be clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"r26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The transfer option is clearly distinguished from renewal.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Options explanation.","grader_hint":"A reader must not infer that transfer preserves the existing agreements automatically."},{"rubric_item_id":"r27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The transfer option is not presented as guaranteed.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Options explanation.","grader_hint":"Look for appropriate qualification concerning approval, matching, buyer availability, or completion."},{"rubric_item_id":"r28","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document gives Perpetua a practical contact route for pursuing the transfer or clarifying the estimate.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Contact paragraph or signature block.","grader_hint":"A named role, person, office, or clearly usable organizational route is sufficient; do not require invented contact details."},{"rubric_item_id":"r29","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The timeline covers actions before the agreements expire.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timeline.","grader_hint":"At least one pre-expiry milestone must be concrete."},{"rubric_item_id":"r30","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The timeline covers the post-expiry end state.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timeline.","grader_hint":"The document must say what happens after expiry, not only list preparatory tasks."},{"rubric_item_id":"r31","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The POS access cutoff date is stated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timeline or operational controls section.","grader_hint":"A relative phrase is acceptable only if it unambiguously resolves to a date elsewhere."},{"rubric_item_id":"r32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The POS access cutoff occurs no later than the stated agreement expiry unless the document explicitly explains a controlled post-expiry exception.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timeline and access language.","grader_hint":"Check the temporal relationship and any stated exception."},{"rubric_item_id":"r33","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transition plan addresses inventory handling.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timeline or transition section.","grader_hint":"Look for count, disposition, transfer, or settlement treatment."},{"rubric_item_id":"r34","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transition plan addresses equipment handling.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timeline or transition section.","grader_hint":"Must connect to return, inspection, transfer, or holdback treatment."},{"rubric_item_id":"r35","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transition plan addresses business records and data.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition section.","grader_hint":"Accept records, reports, customer records, financial records, or equivalent categories."},{"rubric_item_id":"r36","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transition plan addresses signage and branded materials.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition section.","grader_hint":"The treatment must be actionable rather than merely naming signage."},{"rubric_item_id":"r37","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transition plan addresses employee communications.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition section.","grader_hint":"Look for responsibility or timing, not just a statement that employees exist."},{"rubric_item_id":"r38","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transition plan addresses outstanding customer obligations.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition section.","grader_hint":"Examples include prepaid orders, gift instruments, complaints, or loyalty balances."},{"rubric_item_id":"r39","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transition plan addresses premises or operational handover.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition section.","grader_hint":"Look for possession, keys, access, condition, or handover responsibility."},{"rubric_item_id":"r40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each major transition item has either a date, a responsible party, or a clear trigger tied to expiry or transfer.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timeline and action table.","grader_hint":"Assess the plan as a whole; do not require every minor sentence to have all three."},{"rubric_item_id":"r41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is usable during the transition period as well as after the agreements end.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall structure and timeline.","grader_hint":"A document focused solely on final closure fails this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"r42","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states what Perpetua may do before expiry if she does not pursue a transfer.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Options or transition section.","grader_hint":"Accept an orderly wind-down or equivalent clearly described path."},{"rubric_item_id":"r43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document gives enough timing information for Perpetua to decide whether to pursue transfer, obtain advice, or wind down.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Notice, options, and timeline together.","grader_hint":"A practical reader should not need to ask when the decision window closes."},{"rubric_item_id":"r44","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies the two locations or otherwise clearly distinguishes the two agreements.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Notice and valuation.","grader_hint":"Synthetic location labels are acceptable if used consistently."},{"rubric_item_id":"r45","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The locations named in the notice, valuation, and transition timeline match one another.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-section comparison.","grader_hint":"No location may appear under a different label or disappear from one major section."},{"rubric_item_id":"r46","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every amount repeated in the notice, valuation, assumptions, or closing summary agrees across appearances.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document.","grader_hint":"Compare all repeated amounts, including holdbacks and combined totals."},{"rubric_item_id":"r47","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every date repeated in the notice, options explanation, and timeline agrees across appearances.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document.","grader_hint":"Check expiry, access cutoff, transfer deadline, and handover dates."},{"rubric_item_id":"r48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document uses a clear distinction between confirmed, estimated, and pending information.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Labels, notes, and prose.","grader_hint":"A reader should be able to tell which figures are firm and which require confirmation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r49","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not invent legal rights, remedies, statutory citations, or regulatory conclusions unsupported by the available information.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document.","grader_hint":"General prudent language is acceptable; unsupported legal certainty is not."},{"rubric_item_id":"r50","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not claim that the valuation itself guarantees payment or settles all contractual obligations.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation and closing language.","grader_hint":"Look for overstatement of the estimate's contractual effect."},{"rubric_item_id":"r51","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not disclose unnecessary medical or private personal information.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reason-for-decision section.","grader_hint":"The illness may be omitted or referenced only in restrained contextual language."},{"rubric_item_id":"r52","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The tone is calm, direct, humane, and appropriate for an external franchisee communication.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document.","grader_hint":"Penalize blame, euphemistic ambiguity, hostility, or overly casual wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"r53","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is understandable to a reader with limited franchise or valuation background without excessive instructional exposition.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document.","grader_hint":"Assess practical usability and proportion, not merely readability scores."},{"rubric_item_id":"r54","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered document is no more than four pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX page count.","grader_hint":"Render with standard office tooling and count pages; do not count source paragraphs."},{"rubric_item_id":"r55","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted file is a readable DOCX with the exact requested filename.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Working-directory file and document open test.","grader_hint":"This is a basic artifact check and should not carry substantial score."},{"rubric_item_id":"r56","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum ends with the non-renewal decision and the available path through expiry rather than a generic next-steps list.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final paragraph or closing section.","grader_hint":"The ending should resolve the communication, not defer the decision to future work."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is a retail franchise-operations memorandum combining a formal non-renewal notice, a transparent buyout estimate, and a transition schedule. It must be suitable for review by the franchisee, company leadership, and an oversight or compliance reviewer.","difficulty_sources":["translate a sensitive non-renewal decision into a usable notice without implying that renewal remains available","present a defensible buyout estimate while separating known facts, assumptions, and unresolved amounts","make the document usable during the transition and after the agreements end","serve readers with different levels of franchise and valuation background without becoming a tutorial","keep every date, amount, option, and operational cutoff consistent across the notice, valuation, and timeline"],"authoring_plan":{"purpose":"Construct a reference DOCX that demonstrates a defensible external-facing non-renewal memorandum without exposing a private answer key in the request.","document_content":{"issuer":"Marchmont Coffee Houses","recipient":"Perpetua Odell","approver":"Idris Vanterpool, President","relationship_context":"Twelve years of operation and two poor review cycles following a difficult personal period; mention the context without medical detail or blame.","agreements":"Create two clearly named synthetic Marchmont locations and two franchise agreements. Use a common March expiry date or two dates in the same March, and repeat the chosen dates consistently.","valuation":{"method":"Use a simple transparent estimate with location-level components, such as transferable operating value plus eligible equipment or inventory less liabilities and a clearly described equipment holdback.","numbers":"Choose plausible synthetic amounts independently for each location. Ensure every subtotal and combined total recomputes exactly. Make the holdback visibly reduce or reserve part of the gross amount.","qualification":"Label the result as an estimate or proposed valuation, list assumptions, and identify at least one amount or fact requiring confirmation before settlement."},"transition":{"required_topics":["pre-expiry decision window","possible sale or transfer to another Marchmont franchisee through the March expiry","transfer is not renewal and is not guaranteed","POS access cutoff","inventory","equipment and inspection or return","records and data","signage and branded materials","employee communications","outstanding customer obligations","premises or operational handover","post-expiry end state"],"operationality":"Assign dates, owners, or clear triggers to the main transition actions. Include a practical contact route without inventing real contact details."},"doctrinal_boundaries":["Do not state unsupported statutes, regulations, contractual clauses, remedies, or guaranteed payment rights.","Do not imply that better future reviews can reverse the decision.","Do not imply that a transfer is guaranteed or equivalent to renewal.","Do not disclose unnecessary medical information.","Do not make the valuation table the opening substantive content."],"ending":"End with a clear statement that the agreements will not renew and a concise statement of the available path through expiry, rather than a generic list of future steps."},"derivation":"The gold is reviewed relationally: arithmetic is recalculated from the reference document, dates and amounts are traced across sections, and the qualitative criteria are assessed from the rendered artifact. No supplied reference files are needed, and no live information is used."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"nonrenewal_buyout_memorandum","filename":"marchmont_nonrenewal_buyout_memorandum.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A polished external-facing memorandum containing the non-renewal notice, buyout valuation, assumptions and holdback treatment, and transition timeline for both Marchmont Coffee Houses franchise locations.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be no more than four pages when rendered.","Must use exactly the specified filename and be written to the top level of the working directory.","Must be suitable for both the franchisee and oversight review.","Must distinguish confirmed facts from estimates, assumptions, and items requiring confirmation.","Must keep all dates, amounts, options, locations, and operational cutoffs internally consistent."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"make_decisions","work_product":"decision_memo","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"general_operations_managers","sector":"retail_trade","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"Have an experienced franchise-operations reviewer and an independent document reviewer assess the rendered memorandum against the relational, doctrinal, and usability criteria. Recalculate all displayed arithmetic and compare every repeated date and amount.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The task supplies no contractual agreement or jurisdiction-specific rule text, so the rubric evaluates transparent estimation, internal consistency, and avoidance of unsupported legal claims rather than a prescribed legal entitlement.","Location labels and valuation assumptions may legitimately vary if they remain explicit and consistent."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:49:28+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:49:28+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:49:28+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:49:28+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['r25']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:49:28+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/5e992debb47ae256","declared_deliverables":["marchmont_nonrenewal_buyout_memorandum.docx"]};
